---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema, webPageSchema } from '../data/jsonLd';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const title = 'Rivalo Privacy Policy';
const description =
  'How Rivalo collects, uses, stores, and protects your data on iPhone and Apple Watch. Health data, account info, and your privacy choices.';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  jsonLd={[
    webPageSchema(title, description, '/privacy'),
    breadcrumbSchema([
      { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
      { name: 'Privacy Policy', path: '/privacy' }
    ])
  ]}
>
  <LegalPage title="Privacy Policy" updated="June 2, 2026">
    <p>
      Rivalo (“we”, “us”, “our”) builds tools for amateur football players to record matches and
      understand performance over time. This Privacy Policy explains what data we collect, why we
      collect it, how we use it, and the choices you have. By using Rivalo on iPhone or Apple
      Watch, you agree to this policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      Rivalo is a football performance tracking app. Our support contact is
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>. This policy applies to the Rivalo
      mobile apps and the services that power them.
    </p>

    <h2>Data we collect</h2>
    <h3>Account &amp; profile</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Email address and authentication credentials (via Supabase Auth)</li>
      <li>Display name, preferred position, and optional profile fields you provide</li>
      <li>Profile photo if you choose to upload one</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Match &amp; workout data</h3>
    <p>When you record a match on Apple Watch, we may process:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Start and end time, duration, and distance</li>
      <li>Heart rate samples, speed, sprints, intensity, and calories</li>
      <li>GPS route samples used for heatmaps and pitch visualization</li>
      <li>Workout metadata saved to Apple Health (when you grant permission)</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Match context you add</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Opponent, score, outcome (win/draw/loss), competition type</li>
      <li>Goals, assists, notes, position, surface, and court/pitch information</li>
      <li>Personal goals, streaks, rivalries, and records derived from your sessions</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Technical data</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Device type, app version, and basic diagnostic logs needed to operate and secure the service</li>
      <li>API request metadata (timestamps, error codes) — not used for advertising</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we use your data</h2>
    <p>We use your information to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Authenticate you and sync sessions between Apple Watch and iPhone</li>
      <li>Display match summaries, charts, heatmaps, personal records, and progress trends</li>
      <li>Calculate streaks, rivalries, court stats, goals, and post-match insights</li>
      <li>Send local notifications you enable (match summaries, result reminders)</li>
      <li>Maintain, secure, and improve the app and backend infrastructure</li>
      <li>Respond to support requests and legal obligations</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do <strong>not</strong> use your data for third-party advertising or sell personal information.</p>

    <h2>Apple Health &amp; HealthKit</h2>
    <p>
      Rivalo on Apple Watch reads and writes workout-related HealthKit data only to record and
      display your football activity. Health data is used for app functionality — not for
      marketing, advertising, or sale to data brokers. You can revoke Health permissions at any
      time in the Health app or iOS Settings; some features may stop working without them.
    </p>

    <h2>Location data</h2>
    <p>
      Location may be used on Apple Watch to improve distance and route accuracy during outdoor
      matches and to suggest courts you have played at before. Location is tied to your sessions
      and is not used for unrelated tracking or ads.
    </p>

    <h2>How we store &amp; protect data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Account and session data are stored in encrypted cloud infrastructure (Supabase PostgreSQL)</li>
      <li>Authentication tokens are handled via industry-standard JWT flows</li>
      <li>Local credentials on device use the iOS Keychain where applicable</li>
      <li>We apply reasonable technical and organizational measures; no system is 100% secure</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Sharing with third parties</h2>
    <p>We share data only with service providers needed to run Rivalo, such as:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Supabase</strong> — authentication and database hosting</li>
      <li><strong>Apple</strong> — App Store distribution, HealthKit, Watch connectivity, push notification infrastructure</li>
      <li><strong>Cloud hosting</strong> — API and backend services that process your requests</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      These providers process data on our behalf under contractual obligations. We may also disclose
      information if required by law or to protect rights, safety, and security.
    </p>

    <h2>Data retention</h2>
    <p>
      We retain your account and session data while your account is active. If you request account
      deletion, we will delete or anonymize personal data within a reasonable period, except where
      retention is required by law or for legitimate security backups.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights &amp; choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access &amp; correction:</strong> Update profile fields in the app or contact us</li>
      <li><strong>Deletion:</strong> Email {SITE.supportEmail} to request account deletion</li>
      <li><strong>Health permissions:</strong> Manage in iOS Settings → Health → Rivalo</li>
      <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> Manage in iOS Settings → Notifications → Rivalo</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Depending on your region, you may have additional rights (access, portability, objection).
      Contact us and we will respond within applicable legal timeframes.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      Rivalo is not directed at children under 13 (or the minimum age in your jurisdiction). We do
      not knowingly collect personal data from children. Contact us if you believe a child has
      provided data and we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>International transfers</h2>
    <p>
      Your data may be processed in countries other than where you live. We take steps to ensure
      appropriate safeguards when data is transferred internationally.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will post the revised version on this
      page with an updated “Last updated” date. Continued use after changes means you accept the
      updated policy.
    </p>

    <div class="contact-box">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy questions or requests: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </LegalPage>
</BaseLayout>
